{"author":{"id":"585844baa6074d44d241f46aa7c9f21ff46653adf617d7f070fbfe327626c989"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1794735262,"nonce":"112I9jyY/PgnCezZu9WGDk0gVG8=","title":"hxn-gpu-d3d12: a Direct3D 12 driver over the windows crate, binding by hxnsl's HLSL registers","message":"A driver library shaped like Direct3D 12: device, command queue, allocators and lists, heaps and descriptor heaps, root signatures, pipeline state objects, resources and barriers, fences, and a DXGI swapchain on hxn-window's Win32 handle.\n\nShaders are hxnsl's `HLSL`, which D3D12 takes only as bytecode: DXIL from DXC, either during the build (a target step, needing a way for the driver's haxelib to ship one; see the issue on hand-written Haxe in an hxn package) or at run time through dxcompiler.dll, which brings a compiler back into the program. `HLSL_SLOTS` gives each binding's register and space, and the sampler index buffer at `t\u003cgroup\u003e, space255` that indexes the sampler heap; the root signature is built from those.\n\nLike Vulkan, D3D12 needs explicit resource barriers.\n\nPlatform: Windows. CI runners have WARP, the software rasterizer, which runs the checks.","files":null}]}